{
  "description": "#5057 — `delete_attachment` and `rename_attachment`. `attachments` is not one of the snapshot's five arrays, so the `list_attachments` step is what observes the writes. Both commands DO append an op, unlike the other outside-the-snapshot writers pinned so far, so the op-log digest moves too — which is the half a mock that mutates its map silently gets wrong. `add_attachment_with_bytes` is deliberately absent: it writes bytes to disk and answers with a stack-local `fs_path` and a real blake3 `content_hash`, neither of which the mock can reproduce, so it needs a narrower return shape than this fixture would imply. #5057 also undoes the rename here: `applyRevertForOp` had no arm for either attachment op, so an undone rename appended a reverse row and left the filename alone. `delete_attachment` still has no arm, on purpose — its reverse rebuilds an `AddAttachmentPayload` from the original `add_attachment` op, and the mock's `add_attachment_with_bytes` appends none to rebuild from, so that arm arrives when that command is pinned.",
